WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:10.368
A vault is a git repository of markdown notes that your agents read. Decisions and standing orders are written to it, and your workstations keep it in sync.

2
00:00:11.071 --> 00:00:20.138
Open Vaults in the sidebar. The organization vault holds your organization's knowledge and your interests. A project can have a vault of its own.

3
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:29.821
A new project starts with a local folder on one workstation. It is not synced, so back it up yourself, or give the project a git repository.

4
00:00:30.522 --> 00:00:41.125
Choose Register a vault, pick the project, paste the git URL and set the sync interval. Agents never see credentials: the workstation uses its own git access.

5
00:00:41.826 --> 00:00:53.133
Each card shows the git URL, how often it syncs, and every workstation that holds a copy, with its last pull and push. Edit changes the URL or the sync interval.

6
00:00:53.835 --> 00:01:04.246
When the same file changed in two places, sync pauses on that workstation and lists the conflicting files. Fix them in the clone, then choose I resolved it, resume.

7
00:01:04.946 --> 00:01:09.469
That is Vaults: where your agents keep what they know, in repositories you own.
